From 7d2d75edf715d7b0f0bafe35f3a4140c265dd986 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sak-114514 <Sak-114514@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:00:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Keep MTP production measurable within the observed GPU
 headroom

An isolated MTP4 TP3 service now owns the established coding API endpoint.
The DFlash unit and runtime remain intact for rollback. Streaming token-ID
benchmarks and bounded concurrency waves exposed a cold production CUDA Graph
allocation that made 0.91 unsafe at idle; the production unit uses 0.88 and
has completed a cold-prefix 64k request plus an authenticated four-way 50k
wave. The benchmark tools retain both per-client and overlapping-decode rates
so long prefill time is not mislabeled as decode throughput.

Constraint: Three 16GB V100s, existing 8000 API key and coding middleware, no reboot
Rejected: 0.91 production utilization | cold graph capture left only 37-38 MiB idle free
Rejected: 0.92 long-input admission | short four-way wave left 237 MiB before longer contexts
Confidence: medium
Scope-risk: moderate
Reversibility: clean
Directive: Do not raise production utilization from 0.88 without rechecking cold-start graph memory and authenticated four-way 50k headroom
Tested: Ruff check/format; shell syntax; systemd unit verification; matching deployed file hashes; unauthorized HTTP 401; authorized OpenAI chat and Anthropic messages HTTP 200; 64k streamed completion; 4x50k authenticated wave with four running, no waiting or errors
Not-tested: Production 4x60k, 30-minute stability, reboot, full-project CI, token-by-token quality parity
